3.2.2 Technology and Services
The platform is built using a curated set of modern, open-source technologies and cloud services chosen for their robustness, performance, and extensive community support. The architecture employs a multi-language approach to leverage the best tools for specific use cases.

Category
Technology / Service
Purpose
Containerization & Orchestration
Docker, Google Kubernetes Engine (GKE)
Packaging applications into portable containers and managing their lifecycle at scale. GKE provides managed Kubernetes control plane with HPA controllers for automatic scaling.
Backend Framework
Java (Spring Boot), Python (Flask)
Java/Spring Boot serves as the core framework for data processing microservices (data-ingestion, data-processing, data-acquisition, cap-user-service), providing robust enterprise features, web APIs, data persistence, and Kafka integration. Python/Flask powers the cap-pdu-prediction-service to leverage the rich ML/AI ecosystem including scikit-learn, transformers, and RAG capabilities.
API Gateway & Security
Kong Gateway, Firebase Authentication
Kong Gateway provides enterprise-grade API management with centralized routing, Firebase JWT authentication through custom jwt-firebase plugin, CORS policies, rate limiting, and comprehensive monitoring. Firebase Authentication delivers enterprise-grade user management with JWT token validation, eliminating the need for custom authentication infrastructure.
Messaging Bus
Apache Kafka & Apache Zookeeper
A high-throughput, distributed streaming platform used as a message broker to decouple the ingestion and processing services. Kafka topics (dis-pdus) enable asynchronous processing with fault tolerance and message persistence.
Database
PostgreSQL
A powerful, open-source object-relational database system used for persistent storage of processed DIS data (EntityStateRecord, FireEventRecord, DataPduRecord), user data, and session information. Deployed as StatefulSet with 20Gi PVC for data persistence.
Container Registry
GitHub Container Registry (GHCR)
Integrated container image repository maintaining tight integration with source code and CI/CD pipeline. Images follow naming convention ghcr.io/nus-iss-projects/cap-backend-{service-name}/cap-backend-{service-name}:latest for clear traceability.
CI/CD & Automation
GitHub Actions, Kustomize
Automating the build, test, and deployment pipeline with comprehensive rollout verification, automatic rollback capabilities, and DAST security scanning. Kustomize manages environment-specific configurations (local, staging, production) with base configurations and overlays.
Testing & Quality Assurance
JUnit 5, Mockito, Testcontainers, JaCoCo, SonarCloud
Comprehensive testing suite with 75 unit and integration tests across all services. Includes controller tests (@WebMvcTest), service tests with mock repositories, Testcontainers for database integration testing, JaCoCo for code coverage reporting, and SonarCloud for static code analysis and quality metrics.
Monitoring & Observability
Prometheus, Kong Admin API, Health Endpoints
Kong Gateway provides Prometheus metrics collection, while all services expose standardized /health endpoints for readiness and liveness probes. Kong Admin API enables configuration management and monitoring.
Machine Learning & AI
scikit-learn, transformers, RAG System
The cap-pdu-prediction-service leverages Python's ML ecosystem for predictive analytics, vector embeddings, similarity search, and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities for intelligent data analysis and natural language querying.




